WEBVTT

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.690
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.980
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:19.540
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.790
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.390
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:39.700
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.980
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.110
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.980
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.960
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:58.730
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.160
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.670
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:09.900
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:14.100
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.700
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.940
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.320
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.040
It's complete...

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.020
Apsalus, my son!

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.040
Where is the research staff?

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.350
Probably off getting
drunk somewhere.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.090
Let's go. And get into
a normal suit, please.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:32.910
There it is!

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:43.850
Not pulling any
punches, are they?!

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.330
Yes, they are! I know how
powerful that beam <i>really</i> is!

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.750
Let's get out of here!

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.070
You've launched into
the battle, Aina?

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.240
It won't end here, will it?

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.870
Listen, everyone.
I'm leaving the service.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.220
WHAT?!

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.920
Commander?

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.230
Desertion in the
face of the enemy...

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:20.260
They'll shoot you for that!

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.930
I'm not planning on running.
I'm going to stop Aina.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.230
Mr. Pure Love...
You <i>would</i> do this...

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.940
We'll have no choice
except to execute him.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.940
<i>Karen! Take command and</i>
<i>link up with the main force!</i>

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.710
<i>That's my final order to you!</i>

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.780
A lock on?! From Karen's unit?!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:48.020
You want to clear your commander
of these spy charges, don't you?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.920
The Master Chief, too?!

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.590
Won't you change
your mind, sir?

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.560
I can have the entire team
executed, if necessary.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.190
I'm really sorry for
getting you all involved.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.080
That's fine for you, but!

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.510
Master Chief, no!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.480
She did it!

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.850
Every single man I know ends
up leaving me in the end!

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.530
Shiro Amada...

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:40.240
You're the worst
soldier I've ever met.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:44.270
Huh? What does that mean?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.180
No clue.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.180
<i>Scramble Jet Core Boosters!</i>

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.850
<i>Mobile suit forces, damage reports!</i>

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.760
It's getting ready to fire?!
All units, attack!

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.320
<i>Attention Federal Force units!</i>

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:11.530
<i>This is Aina Sahalin,</i>
<i>the pilot of this mobile armor.</i>

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.870
<i>I request a temporary truce.</i>

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.570
Are you mad?!

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.770
Shoot their command center
and you'll end this!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.780
That would still leave
them with air superiority.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:28.980
It's too risky to leave those
fighters shooting at the <i>Kergeren!</i>

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.430
Do as you wish...

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:38.030
The attack just
now was a warning!

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.900
- <i>You okay?</i>
- <i>Yeah, I think so.</i>

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.530
<i>As long as that burn</i>
<i>line isn't crossed...</i>

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.610
<i>...no further attacks</i>
<i>will be made.</i>

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.030
We've got video back!

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.270
No sign of damage from
the previous attack.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.980
What's going on here?
What are they up to?

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.470
I knew it was Aina!

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.520
This is how Aina fights!

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:03.050
<i>The sick and wounded from our</i>
<i>base will now be evacuated.</i>

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.490
I'm begging you.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.150
For this moment at least,
please stop the fighting!

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.030
For crying out loud...

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:17.560
She's another Newbie at heart?
Don't underestimate the military...

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.000
I must deny your request!

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.250
Don't you understand why?
A truce at gunpoint...

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.050
<i>Our forces will</i>
<i>not be intimidated!</i>

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.850
If you can't believe me, then...

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.390
<i>Ninety-eight! Ninety-seven!</i>

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.460
You little!

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:50.840
Please watch. This is <i>my</i> war!

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.020
Very well.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.690
Thank you!

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.380
Have the GM Snipers stand by.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.150
But you just...

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:13.160
I don't recall
making any promises.

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:15.620
Aye, sir...

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:19.930
<i>We're headed for the</i>
<i>rendezvous! Good luck!</i>

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:38.350
<i>Two... One... Zero!</i>

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.660
No, don't!

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.470
GINIAS!!!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.220
They drew first blood.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.620
Can't you get a lock on
that thing's cockpit?!

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.560
Sniper 2, still moving
into position!

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.490
Open fire on
that med-evac ship.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.460
No difference
between either side...

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.230
Get that coolant
pipe attached, ASAP!

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.570
<i>Long beam rifle,</i>
<i>stand-by, okay!</i>

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.610
Coolant system, okay!

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.850
Keep that coolant running!

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:50.910
And that's what your trusted
Federal Forces do in the end.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:53.720
But, it was because...

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:56.490
Wake up! Wake up and LOOK!

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:03.690
Fire.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:14.170
Is that a sacrifice
for your ideals?!

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:34.890
God damn you all!

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.100
Shiro?!

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.520
She really fired it...

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.720
<i>Incoming shock wave! Sanders!</i>
<i>Protect the hovertruck!</i>

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.090
<i>Aye, aye!</i>

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:15.730
<i>Eledore! Michel!</i>

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.000
The armor's getting hot! If any
of our ammo cooks off, then!

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.130
Shut up! Start praying!

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:25.010
Oh, B.B., who art in heaven!

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.050
I wasn't serious, you idiot!

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.710
I don't care what
it takes, just save me!

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.050
<i>Did we make it?</i>

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.090
<i>Is everyone all right?</i>

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.520
<i>What about the main force?</i>

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:55.110
Aina, is this some
sort of a joke?

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:01.150
No. This is my answer.

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:09.250
They missed...

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:12.190
She really went and did it...

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.690
Is that Sniper
in position yet?!

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:17.390
Seven more minutes...
No, five more minutes, please!

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.070
I thought you understood now
how ruthless our enemy is!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:31.510
Yes. But revenge isn't going to
bring those soldiers back to life.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:36.680
I see we don't speak the
same language anymore.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:41.980
I stopped listening to you
a long time ago. But...

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.160
Ridiculous!

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.820
Love is just an illusion,
created by your body's glands!

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.300
It's what drove Mother
to abandon us both!

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:00.500
How I pity you...
Is that the reason?

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:04.310
Why you built this
iron womb for yourself?

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.740
<i>I'm in position.</i>
<i>One minute to E-CAP charge.</i>

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.550
Don't talk like you
understand anything!

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.590
This is war!

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:17.660
No. This is a personal matter.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.620
You damned little!

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.760
Let's surrender.
Let the burden be taken away.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.360
Aina!

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:53.590
Aina! Please wake up!

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:55.760
Don't die, Aina!

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:58.120
It was you?!

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.900
It was your fault my
sister had to die?!

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.300
This can't be happening...

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:17.650
No... Aina...

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.520
A farewell gift from your brother.
You shall die together.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.720
A brother who kills
his own <i>sister?!</i>

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:34.970
All I want... is to kill you!

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:42.400
Interesting. I've always wanted
to see a ghost, if only once.

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:53.750
Farewell, Aina.
I didn't hate you.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:58.120
No... Live!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:13.970
No!

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:24.950
Good!

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:34.790
<i>Did they get it?!</i>

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:37.130
<i>All units, damage reports!</i>

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:43.560
The main force is okay?
Talk about dumb luck!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.870
<i>08th Team has returned.</i>

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:52.140
Karen? Unit 8-1's captured an
enemy pilot. Move in to escort him.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.480
No.

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.110
Whatever the reason, he still
deserted in the face of the enemy.

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:59.620
I thought I ordered
you to execute him.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.120
Execute him?!

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:04.780
First of all, I doubt the ensign will
turn that female pilot over to us.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.820
Hurry up with the recovery
of that mobile armor!

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.020
I never heard anything
about an execution order!

00:16:12.230 --> 00:16:14.360
This is just a lynching!

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.630
Rob... Sally... Mike...

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:21.340
I lost a lot of good
people in this battle.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:24.610
Which means one more
won't matter much.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.880
No, sir.
Just the opposite!

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:32.150
Karen! Assemble the team.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:33.980
We'll be running a
different mission now.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:34.920
<i>Aye, sir!</i>

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:40.450
I believe I heard you order the
shooting down of a med-evac ship before.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:44.060
There are rules
you follow, even in war.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.930
That's what I believe, at least.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:53.000
Those offices at Jaburo
are pretty comfortable.

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:56.770
And I told you I never
could stand air conditioning.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.980
Your new orders are to
stop that mobile armor...

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.020
...and take Shiro Amada
into custody!

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:07.550
Shiro? Shiro?

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:10.420
Aina?

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:18.890
I'm glad. I really am...

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:25.900
Shiro!

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:32.710
We're together again.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:37.240
You lived.
You lived through that...

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:51.860
The watch my brother gave me is
what brought us together again.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:02.240
An engineer like my brother
won't let it end this way.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:05.470
The Apsalus will
definitely rise again.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.170
Let's go.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.550
Let's end all this
with our own hands.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:15.980
We can't run from
facing your brother.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:18.250
You're right.

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:22.320
You've gotten stronger.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.870
You were really
cool before, Commander!

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:35.840
Quiet! Just shut up.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.910
We have to get there
before that Sniper...

00:18:38.980 --> 00:18:41.110
...or else the ensign's
a dead man!

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:46.410
At the very least, I want to
court-martial that idiot!

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.250
- Now move it!
- Aye, sir!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.090
Handle the right-hand
control, okay?

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.260
Right.

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:03.330
If we just take out
the beam generator...

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:04.740
Gotcha.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.370
Let's get around to
the beam cannon barrel!

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.770
The Ez8 is moving!

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:12.210
Sniper 2!

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.010
<i>Confirmed!</i>

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:13.740
<i>Fire!</i>

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.180
<i>Roger.</i>

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:20.880
If I just had a little time!
Dammit!

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.900
Aina! You're alive?!

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:42.610
I'll put you out of
your misery soon!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.650
That's for crushing my
dream of destroying Jaburo!

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:58.650
And next comes you two!

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:04.360
He wants to take both us...

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.430
...and your main force out
with a full power blast!

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.270
Aina...

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.600
I'm going to
kill your brother.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:15.230
He's hurt us both too much,
and he's left us no choice now.

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:21.140
Farewell, Big Brother.

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:26.020
We have to keep it from firing
its main gun at all costs!

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:32.020
Now take my dream!

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:51.580
Evacuate! All personnel, evacuate!

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:55.350
It's too late.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.140
A double-suicide...

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:24.080
It's not true!
Right, Chief?!

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:26.200
The commander's
not dead, right?!

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.210
Of course not.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.210
Yeah, of course not!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.290
C'mon! Let's go.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:39.880
Eledore...

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:43.190
I dunno what happened before,
but I'm sure Newbie's forgiven you.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:45.890
You're so sure of that?

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:49.430
Sure I'm sure!
We're friends, right?

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:54.340
Come on! Hey, Newbie!
Come out already!

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:56.940
Commander!

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:00.040
Please come out, sir!

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.650
Commander!

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:12.590
Commander! Commander!
Where are you?!

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:19.030
<i>"Not long after it happened,</i>
<i>the war ended."</i>

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:45.160
Asayake o mitsumeteru anata o,
Gazing at the morning glow,

00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:48.870
watashi wa miteta
I saw you there.

00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:54.310
Two of us...

00:22:54.340 --> 00:23:00.370
futari ni, tari nai mono o kazoe tara
Two of us, finding nothing else to do, just started counting...

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:04.740
Nandaka okashiku natte,
Finding it strangely funny,

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:07.720
koe o agete waratta...
we burst out laughing...

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:16.960
Nayan da hibi no kotae nante
What is the answer for our troubling days?

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:23.250
Arukidasu koto shikanai yone
It's nothing that a little walk can't help, right?

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:30.390
Kasa ne au samishisa wa,
This overlapping loneliness,

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:36.440
nukumori o oshiete kureta
teach me about it warmly...

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:37.320
<i>"P.S. In the end, we never</i>
<i>did find the commander."</i>

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:41.450
Dakiaeba namida sae,
Let's embrace each other even in tears,

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:43.380
<i>"But, I still believe he's alive."</i>

00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:45.010
wake mo naku... itoshii
unconditionally... That would be lovely.

00:23:45.010 --> 00:23:46.710
<i>"My love to you, B.B."</i>

00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:50.220
wake mo naku... itoshii
unconditionally... That would be lovely.

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:51.850
You're heavy.

00:23:52.130 --> 00:23:54.630
Mirai no futari ni
The future for the both of us,

00:23:54.630 --> 00:23:55.290
Then we'll share the burden. Together.

00:23:55.290 --> 00:23:57.670
Ima o wara warenai youni
In order for our smiles today not to disappear,

